  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "block_id": "h1-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Mission Context Packets",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Mission context packets are the deterministic bridge from a mission envelope to the bounded context an agent run should receive.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "They are not the canonical governance ledger. Canonical sources remain files:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `docs/governance/**/*.md` - `docs/schemas/**/*.json` - `docs/audits/**/*.jsonl` - `.rig/work/**/*.jsonl` when present - receipt stores when present",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "DuckDB may be used later as a rebuildable analytical index over those files, but the packet itself is compiled from canonical inputs and remains content-light.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Contract",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Executable model:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `rig_relay.governance.mission_context_packet.MissionContextPacket` - `rig_relay.governance.mission_context_packet.MissionContextPacketReceipt` - `rig_relay.governance.mission_context_compiler.MissionContextCompiler`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Schemas:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `docs/schemas/rig.mission_context_packet.v1.schema.json` - `docs/schemas/rig.mission_context_packet_receipt.v1.schema.json`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Design Rules",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- Deterministic serialization. - Strict schema validation. - Mission-envelope linkage is optional but supported. - No raw prompts, stdout, stderr, patches, diffs, or secrets. - Source references are explicit and content-light. - DuckDB is a cache/index only, never the canonical source of truth.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Compiler Inputs",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- an explicit `MissionEnvelope` - explicit allow-listed source paths or allow-listed source roots - optional dirty-file states - optional required checks",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-15",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Compiler Outputs",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `MissionContextPacket` - `MissionContextPacketReceipt`",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The receipt captures packet and mission envelope fingerprints, counts, and the declared index backend.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Ordering Rules",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- source discovery is deterministic - source refs are emitted in lexicographic path order - explicit mission-envelope ordering is preserved for the envelope-owned path/check lists",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Deferred Runtime Integration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This compiler is a prototype. Runtime execution should not consume it yet. The runtime adapter and execution layer remain separate until the packet contract stabilizes.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Relationship To Mission Envelope",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The mission envelope supplies the mission identity and immediate runtime boundary. The context packet compiles the relevant supporting context for that mission from canonical files and safe state summaries.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The packet can exist without higher-order ADR or sprint orchestration.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
  ],
